<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hill of Ward</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tlachtga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hill of Ward, anciently Tlachtga, is a hill near Athboy in County Meath, Ireland, crowned by a ringfort with multiple banks. In early Irish tradition it was the site of a great fire festival at Samhain, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was a place of royal assemblies. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigernan-ua-ruairc">Tigernán Ua Ruairc</a>, king of Breifne, was killed there in 1172 during a parley with Hugh de Lacy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hill-of-ward.jpg" alt="Hill of Ward" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kieran Campbell · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hill_of_Ward_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1923643.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
